ounter-swing, same hoe/spade low beside thigh, NOTHING being carried except tool.\n6 SAME TANG WALK CONTACT B: right leg forward/left leg back, exactly opposite stride to row5, identical character/outfit/tool/scale.\nDo not omit or merge rows. Idle rows stand normally; walk pairs visibly show the two opposite leg positions with bent knees and heel/toe placement. Do not reuse any food baskets or timber bundles from references. No work strike poses; these are unladen villagers idle or traveling between orders. Render detailed historical materials faithful to reference. Only extremely faint tight contact shadows.",
